= MaterialX Volume Texture =

#context: vop
#type: node

"""Resamples a 3D voxel field from an atlas exported by Labs VolumeTexture Export."""

== Overview ==

Labs VolumeTexture Export writes a volume as a grid of slices packed into one
image. This node reads that image back: for a given position it picks the two
slices either side of it and blends between them, reconstructing the field the
atlas was baked from.

It feeds a volume shader, not a surface one. Drive `kma_volume`'s scattering or
emission with it, or an EDF or VDF feeding `mtlxvolume`. The usual subject is a
uniform volume — the Cube a Karma Fog Box creates, for instance — where the
shader supplies the field the volume does not carry itself.

Export the atlas with __Up Axis__ set to Y, which is the axis this node slices
along.

== The bounding box ==

The slice is chosen from the position inside a bounding box. MaterialX has no
access to one, so this node reads the box from two primvars and works out the
position itself. They must describe the box the atlas was exported from, which
is the prim's own `extent` whenever the geometry matches that box:

{{{
primvars:bboxmin   float3   constant
primvars:bboxmax   float3   constant
}}}

Because they are constant primvars rather than shader parameters, one material
can be bound to many prims and each still uses its own box.

@parameters

Volume Texture:
    #id: file
    The atlas image from Labs VolumeTexture Export.

U Tile:
    #id: utile
    Columns of slices in the atlas. Must match the export.

V Tile:
    #id: vtile
    Rows of slices in the atlas. Must match the export.

BBox Min Primvar:
    #id: bboxmin
    Name of the constant primvar holding the minimum corner of the box.

BBox Max Primvar:
    #id: bboxmax
    Name of the constant primvar holding the maximum corner of the box.

@outputs

out:
    The field sampled at the shading position, blended from the two nearest
    slices.
